{"content":"**Fixed — the payload temp file is now repo-relative, matching the cited precedent.**

`open_pr` in `guestApplyStep` (js/smAgent.js) writes `gt_pr_payload_tmp_<ts>-<sanitized branch>.json` into the working directory — the same shape as scm.js's `updatePrBody` (`pr_body_update_tmp_<id>.md`, js/common/scm.js:499) that the block cites — instead of the POSIX-only `/tmp/gt-pr-…`. Non-POSIX dmtools hosts no longer lose the PR-creation step at `file_write`, and the precedent claim in the comment is now accurate. The `finally { file_delete(...) }` best-effort cleanup is retained, and the payload still travels entirely via `--input <file>` (zero untrusted bytes in the shell string).
