- `_resumeTailSteps` (the resume-after-open-pr path) ends the same way, pinning the recorded arm sha as the head.

The terminal op is rendered by the wiring (`guestApplyStep` case `transplanted_marker`) from the runtime ctx — the created PR number and merge sha exist only after the steps above ran — so the posted marker carries `transplant: <newPrNumber>`, `merged: <mergedSha>`, `head: <usedSha>`.

Pinned by a wiring-faithful replay in `test_guestTransplant.js` (round 3 suite): the fresh sequence's own posted comments (arm marker + terminal marker, rendered via the same `transplantMarkerComment` the wiring calls) are fed back through `parseTransplantMarker` → `transplantSequence` — the reopened source reads `noop / already-transplanted`, zero steps. Same replay for the resume path: the tail leaves `transplanted` behind, second tick no-ops. Your replay's `duplicate transplant: YES` is now `noop`.
","path":"/home/runner/work/dmtools-agents/dmtools-agents/outputs/review_replies/thread_12.md"}

{"content":"**Fixed — transplant markers are now machineAuthor-authenticated at parse time** (`parseTransplantMarker`, `js/common/guestTransplant.js`, round 3), following the repo's own gh-828 doctrine you cited.

