The `guest-transplant` rule description (`sm_github.json`) no longer claims in-repo enforcement: it now names the project-side integration point (`guestValidationDispatchPlan(jobs, smGuestTransplant.gate, workflowFile)` called by the consuming project's validate leg on the fetched job graph, failing the leg on `ok: false`) and states plainly that a project skipping the hook has **no gate enforcement**. The checker's docblock in `js/common/guestTransplant.js` carries the same contract. The "impossible by construction" wording is scoped to the transport property it actually covers (no fork-owned ref is ever targeted — command builders are byte-pinned and UT-gated), not to the gate ordering.
